[Music]  new data is in regarding the recovery of  small businesses who say their  definition for success  will be when they're able to pay all of  their employees a full salary without  concern  this data is from cabbage it's an  american express company that is  tracking small business growth across  the u.s through next year  it found 57 percent of the small  businesses surveyed  say their businesses are now fully open  as local and federal shutdowns ease  keep in mind there are 30 million small  businesses across the nation  about 90 percent of them have fewer than  20 employees and 80 percent have fewer  than 10 employees  small businesses in general account for  50 percent of our non-farm gdp and 66  of all new jobs that are created  co-founder of cabbage catherine petralia  says there are great government programs  to help these small businesses recover  only a small percentage of small  businesses took advantage of the  paycheck protection program  under the cares act and there's now a  second round available so if businesses  took the first round  and they may be eligible for the second  round and if you never took a route if  you never borrowed under the program  most of those loans are going to become  grants and it's a great opportunity  to get some capital that will help  bridge the gap  also from the data a third of the  businesses surveyed plan to expand their  digital operations to either supplement  or  altogether replace in-person operations  overall many agreed they would consider  adopting new technologies to run their  companies more efficiently  you can read the full report on our  website at 8newsnow.com

